WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:21.053
Each princess had her own small garden.

2
00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:25.543
One princess made her flower bed in the shape of a whale.

3
00:00:25.544 --> 00:00:29.945
Another princess made her garden in the shape of a shell.

4
00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:36.190
The sisters filled their gardens with odd things they had found in sunken ships.

5
00:00:36.191 --> 00:00:39.546
But the Little Mermaid's garden was simple.

6
00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:44.401
It had only red flowers and a statue of a human boy.

7
00:00:44.402 --> 00:00:49.568
The statue had been her mother's, and the Little Mermaid loved it.

8
00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:56.152
While her sisters played in their gardens, the Little Mermaid sat quietly in hers.

9
00:00:56.153 --> 00:01:01.379
Looking at the boy, she wondered about humans and the world above.

10
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:07.117
"What is it like in the Upper World?" she asked her grandmother one day.

11
00:01:07.118 --> 00:01:13.380
"Oh, little one, there is so much to see!" said the Wise Mermaid.

12
00:01:13.381 --> 00:01:19.191
"There are thick forests of trees that turn colors when the air turns cold.

13
00:01:19.192 --> 00:01:23.498
Soon after, their leaves fall to the ground.

14
00:01:23.499 --> 00:01:26.498
Then the snow comes."

15
00:01:26.499 --> 00:01:31.314
"Snow?" said the Little Mermaid. "What's that?"

16
00:01:31.315 --> 00:01:37.669
"Snow is made of thousands of small ice flakes," replied her grandmother.

17
00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:42.407
"In winter these flakes fall from the sky.

18
00:01:42.408 --> 00:01:46.974
But in summer green grass covers the ground.

19
00:01:46.975 --> 00:01:51.783
And the flowers give off a lovely scent."

20
00:01:51.784 --> 00:01:56.188
"It sounds wonderful," the Little Mermaid said.

21
00:01:56.189 --> 00:02:00.078
"Here our trees always look the same.

22
00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:03.345
And the flowers have no smell at all."

23
00:02:03.346 --> 00:02:06.405
The Wise Mermaid told her more.

24
00:02:06.406 --> 00:02:14.668
"In the Upper World, you can look up in the sky and clearly see the sun, moon, and stars.

25
00:02:14.669 --> 00:02:21.522
And birds fly from tree to tree, singing lovely songs."

26
00:02:21.523 --> 00:02:26.596
"Tell me about the animals, Grandmother," the Little Mermaid begged.

27
00:02:26.597 --> 00:02:29.476
"Some fly, as I said.

28
00:02:29.477 --> 00:02:34.786
But many have four legs and walk on the ground.

29
00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:40.923
Humans walk on two legs, and they are very good at building things.

30
00:02:40.924 --> 00:02:45.831
They make lots of houses, which become towns."

31
00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:49.236
The Little Mermaid wanted to hear more.

32
00:02:49.237 --> 00:02:52.630
"They also build ships, don't they?"

33
00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:57.299
"Oh yes, little one," her grandmother said.

34
00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:01.185
"But you already know that."

35
00:03:01.186 --> 00:03:05.527
"I know, but I love to hear about humans.

36
00:03:05.528 --> 00:03:09.763
They come so close to us, sailing above.

37
00:03:09.764 --> 00:03:13.371
But their world seems so far away."

38
00:03:13.372 --> 00:03:18.654
"Yes, humans are very different from us," said her grandmother.

39
00:03:18.655 --> 00:03:22.219
"They don't live as long as sea folk.

40
00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.453
We live for three hundred years!

41
00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:28.019
But humans have souls."

42
00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:32.126
"What is a soul?" the Little Mermaid asked.

43
00:03:32.127 --> 00:03:36.929
"I don't know, little one," the Wise Mermaid replied.

44
00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.262
"I have heard a soul can live forever.

45
00:03:41.263 --> 00:03:45.283
But humans don't really know what a soul is either.

46
00:03:45.284 --> 00:03:50.728
Whatever it is, I think it must be something special."

47
00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:54.900
"I want to know everything about humans!"

48
00:03:54.901 --> 00:04:01.081
"When you are 15 years old, you will see," said her grandmother.

49
00:04:01.082 --> 00:04:06.088
"You'll swim to the surface and watch the ships sail by."

50
00:04:06.089 --> 00:04:11.515
"But I want to go now!" the Little Mermaid pleaded.

51
00:04:11.516 --> 00:04:18.282
"Be patient—your turn will come in five years," said her grandmother, smiling.

52
00:04:18.283 --> 00:04:25.811
"But you will find, dear, that our home down here is better than any place else."

53
00:04:25.812 --> 00:04:30.812
The years passed and the Little Mermaid's sisters went to the Upper World.

54
00:04:30.813 --> 00:04:33.878
But she had to wait.

55
00:04:33.879 --> 00:04:39.712
So on clear nights, she looked up at the moon and stars.

56
00:04:39.713 --> 00:04:46.500
Whenever a shadow swept across them, she knew it was a ship passing overhead.

57
00:04:46.501 --> 00:04:53.114
Eagerly the Little Mermaid stretched her white arms up toward the bottom of the ship.

58
00:04:53.115 --> 00:05:01.967
Someday she would touch the world above.
